rs most. Day to day, you will: Perform exploratory testing of new and existing features to uncover edge cases. Run regression tests to ensure platform stability before releases. Maintain, write, and scale our automated test suites. Reproduce user-reported issues and provide technical support to resolve them. Collaborate with developers to share product knowledge and diagnose system bugs. Work with product managers to estimate the priority and business impact of issues. What you’ll bring Strong communication skills and the ability to explain technical problems clearly. Independence, self-discipline, and a habit of learning new technologies on your own. A collaborative approach to working with distributed engineering teams. What you’ll need Proven experience testing commercial software applications. Proficiency in Java or Kotlin sufficient to write test applications and read source code. Fluency in spoken and written English. Practical familiarity with build tools (like Maven, Gradle, or Bazel), databases, and Docker containers. Experience testing software across different operating systems alongside basic system administration skills. What success looks like Success in this role means earning the trust of your team through sound testing decisions and leaving our codebase cleaner and more stable than you found it. You will move past simple task lists to take real ownership of product quality, helping the team ship reliable updates without compromising speed. Ultimately, success is defined by preventing regressions and ensuring enterprise developers have a seamless experience using our tools. Why join JetBrains? Strong base salary. We offer competitive pay that reflects your skills and experience. Flexible work location. Enjoy the freedom to work from home or from the office. Remote work. Spend up to 30 days per year working remotely from abroad. Extra time off. More days to relax, recharge, and do the things you love. Medical insurance allowance. Enjoy peace of mind for you and your family Learning and development opportunities. Access to conferences, courses, and language classes. Relocation support. We help make your move as smooth and stress-free as possible. Language classes. Pick up the local language or sharpen your English skills. Fuel your day. Enjoy a hot meal or receive a lunch allowance on workdays. Mental health support. To help you feel your best, we provide easy access to professional mental health services. Sports benefit. Enjoy an on-site gym or sports club stipend. Internal events. Join company-wide celebrations and team gatherings. *Some benefits may vary depending on location. Arbeitsorte Karte anzeigen Christoph-Rapparini-Bogen 23, 80639 München Cuvrystraße 53, 10997 Berlin Unternehmensdarstellung: JetBrains GmbH Hauptsitz München Betriebsgröße 1000+ In diesem Dokument befinden sich aus Sicherheitsgründen keine Kontaktdaten des Arbeitgebers. Wenn Sie diese sehen möchten, lösen Sie bitte die Sicherheitsfrage und laden Sie das PDF erneut. Informationen zur Bewerbung Fußbereich Stelle betreut durch die BA Referenz-Nr.: 10001-1003780573-S Verstoß melden",
